anker-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py` was rounding with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That's why the test expecting `2.665` to round to `2.66` failed.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). I haven't merged it, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\nWhen I looked up FIN-212, the advisory tool didn't recognise it, so I went by the docstring and the test.", "type": "text"}]}]}